  "note": "karpenter-cost-estimate.py --nodepool apps-serving. 17 distinct apps-serving nodes churned through this ~21min window against a TEI peak of 16 and api peak of 3. D16 is essentially flat vs r200 ($0.00086) despite this point showing real saturation (p95 exploded, error rate up) -- cost per query didn't rise to reflect the latency/error degradation, meaning D16 alone would understate how much worse this point actually is. The Matrix in Sec3 needs the latency/error columns alongside D16, not D16 in isolation, or this looks like a non-event.",
  "revision_note": "Revised 2026-09-24 under the data-file rule (figures.yaml meta.data_files): a data file holds readings, not results. Removed, all typed by hand rather than produced by any tool: M9_serving_gross_usd (now the totals_by_nodepool sum over rows anyone can re-add), serving_floor_rate_usd_per_hour / serving_floor_cost_for_window_usd / M9_net_of_floor_usd (a per-point floor netting, which D2 retired in favour of subtracting the floor once at campaign level, and which rested on a rate retired twice), D16 per 1k queries (a result; it lives in figures.yaml as d16_gross_r500), and queries_served (a choice between two counts, now recorded as the two readings the generator printed). The note above was written against the netted generation: its D16 values and the comparisons drawn from them are superseded, and the gross ordering across the five points is in 02-inference Sec3."
